---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ProjectCard from '../components/ProjectCard.astro';
import { consultancy, person } from '../config/brand';

const projects = (await getCollection('projects')).sort((a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order);
---

<Base>
  <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <p class="label">Adelaide · 34.9°S 138.6°E</p>
    <h1 id="hero-title">Justin <em>Powell</em></h1>
    <p class="lede">
      I'm not a trained developer, but I spend most days building software with AI.
    </p>
    <a class="scroll-cue" href="#projects">Projects ↓</a>
  </section>

  <section id="projects" class="projects" aria-labelledby="projects-title">
    <div class="projects-head">
      <p class="label">01 / Projects</p>
      <h2 id="projects-title">Projects</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="cards">
      {projects.map((p) => <ProjectCard project={p} />)}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="consulting" class="panel glass" aria-labelledby="consulting-title">
    <p class="label">02 / Consulting</p>
    <h2 id="consulting-title">Consulting</h2>
    <p>
      I run {consultancy.name}, a small consultancy for founders and COOs at B2B SaaS companies. I build one revenue system at a time, for a fixed price, in the stack you already use. Most builds are live in about 30 days.
    </p>

    <h3>Example builds</h3>
    <ul class="builds">
      <li><strong>Inbound engine:</strong> new leads get enriched, routed and followed up, without anyone copying data between tools.</li>
      <li><strong>Renewal pipeline:</strong> renewals show up in HubSpot months ahead, each with an owner and a next step.</li>
      <li><strong>Forecasting and internal tools:</strong> a forecast you can check line by line, plus the small tools your team keeps asking for.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="proof">
      <p>
        I've been the first RevOps hire through one IPO and two acquisitions. Clients include UpGuard, Sherlok and Elita. {consultancy.name} is a {consultancy.partner}.
      </p>
      <p>
        At Magnific (formerly Freepik), I led the AI rebuild of a legacy product. It went from zero to hundreds of thousands of weekly users and drove a third of all new subscriptions.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button primary" href={person.bookingUrl} data-track="book-call">Book a scoping call</a>
      <a class="button secondary" href={consultancy.url}>More at {new URL(consultancy.url).hostname}</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="about" class="panel glass" aria-labelledby="about-title">
    <p class="label">03 / About</p>
    <h2 id="about-title">About</h2>
    <p>
      I'm {person.firstName}. I'm American, I live in Adelaide, and I've worked in RevOps since 2012, in the US, the UK, Germany and Australia. I've also managed product and tech teams at EyeEm and at Slidesgo, which is part of Magnific.
    </p>
    <p>
      I studied physics for four years, first at the University of Arizona and then at the University of Utah, and graduated with a degree in economics and a minor in physics. Physics taught me to measure something before I try to change it. I still work that way, whether it's a CRM or a LiDAR survey.
    </p>
    <p>
      In JavaScript, a <code>falsy</code> value acts false without actually being false. That's kind of how I feel when I talk about being a “developer”.
    </p>
    <p>
      The planet behind this page is Mars, rendered from real NASA and USGS data. On a computer, you're watching it live from a real orbit about 200 km up, moving as fast as a spacecraft would, with the Sun where it really is right now. On a phone, you get a still from the same renderer. The mountains are stretched 2.5 times taller so they show up from that height. I built it because I love space and physics, and I wanted my site to show the kind of work I do.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="contact" class="panel glass" aria-labelledby="contact-title">
    <p class="label">04 / Contact</p>
    <h2 id="contact-title">Contact</h2>
    <p>If you want to talk about one of my projects, email is best.</p>
    <p class="email">
      <span class="label">Email</span>
      <a href={`mailto:${person.email}`}>{person.email}</a>
    </p>
    <p>For consulting, the quickest way to start is a 30-minute call. I work Adelaide hours, and the booking page shows times in your time zone.</p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button primary" href={person.bookingUrl} data-track="book-call">Book a call</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  section {
    margin-inline: var(--gutter);
  }

  .hero {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    align-content: start;
    gap: 22px;
    min-height: calc(100svh - 64px);
    padding-top: clamp(48px, 12vh, 140px);
    max-width: 44rem;
  }

  .scroll-cue {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    bottom: 72px;
    font: 400 var(--step--1) / 1 var(--data);
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--muted);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .scroll-cue:hover {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: var(--step-4);
    line-height: 0.92;
  }

  .lede {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--muted);
    max-width: 34rem;
  }

  .actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 14px 26px;
    margin-top: 6px;
  }



  .panel {
    display: grid;
    gap: 20px;
    max-width: 62rem;
    margin-bottom: 40px;
    padding: clamp(24px, 4vw, 48px);
  }

  .panel > p,
  .proof p {
    max-width: 65ch;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-3);
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }

  h3 {
    font: 500 var(--step--1) / 1.2 var(--data);
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }


  .builds {
    display: grid;
    gap: 12px;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .builds li {
    padding-left: 18px;
    border-left: 1px solid var(--glass-line);
  }

  .builds strong {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 2px;
    font: 500 var(--step--1) / 1.6 var(--data);
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }





  .proof {
    display: grid;
    gap: 14px;
    padding-top: 20px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--grid);
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .projects {
    display: grid;
    gap: 22px;
    max-width: 62rem;
    margin-block: 72px 112px;
  }

  .cards {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(min(100%, 22rem), 1fr));
    gap: 18px;
  }

  .email {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 8px 14px;
  }

  .email a {
    font: 400 var(--step-0) / 1.4 var(--data);
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration-color: var(--glass-line);
    text-underline-offset: 5px;
    user-select: all;
  }

  #about {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
</style>
